ion auto the city  have expressed concern all realized that  the brexit that's coming may limits  access or membership of the single  market and the customs union and this is  one of the responses is that a fair  interpretation they're beginning to  worry a little bit about their  industries I think it's important when  we look at what we're going to be  negotiate  we want to get the right deal for the UK  I think it's important that we look at  this not in a sense of sort of either  where we're trying to if you like see  which bits of membership we can keep  we're going to be an independent  sovereign country outside of the  European Union and the question is what  is the right relationship for us to have  with the EU now I'm very clear about  that I want the relationship that gives  the best possible opportunity for our  businesses to trade in with and to  operate within the European Union and of  course for European businesses to be  able to trade with us and operate within  the UK and what we're doing as a  government what I've done is sat down  with businesses lit both large and small  here in the UK I've sat down with  American investors in to the UK and talk  to them about where their priorities are  where their concerns are it's not all  good to be plain sailing there will be  some bumps in the road but what I want  to ensure is that we get the right deal  for the UK look at the history of your  party of this conference and one of your  predecessors almost exactly 30 years ago  signed the deal the single European act  brought Britain into the single market  was seen as warned of Margaret  Thatcher's great successes what is the  problem for you with membership of the  single market that was such a  achievement of your party and your  predecessor well feisal I think it as  I've just said it's important for us to  consider what the position of the UK is  going to be we will be an independent  sovereign country and the question is  what is our relationship what 